# Conclusion

The application was vulnerable to **Mass Assignment**, allowing arbitrary modification of internal object properties.

By adding the hidden `roleid` attribute to the JSON request, it was possible to escalate privileges from a normal user to an administrator without exploiting authentication or guessing credentials.

This vulnerability highlights the importance of restricting which properties may be modified by clients and avoiding automatic binding between user-controlled input and sensitive server-side objects.

